From dd147cae0e85f9e39855d0d130da19e782f7eecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Haas <kevinroberthaas@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T-2980: Reproduce reviewed wagons across Python versions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Use explicit compensated floating-point sums in hardware construction and
covered normals/material normalization. Native Python 3.11 now reproduces
the original raw parts and all three reviewed GLBs exactly, as does 3.12.
Keep every original input/output hash guard and recipe unchanged; refresh
only source-code provenance hashes in sidecars and SOURCE manifests.

Changelog: none — authoring-only reproducibility repair; shipped wagon geometry, materials and appearance are byte-exact. Existing vehicle entries describe the parked replacements.
